        "evidence_hash": "8e1f53f3bb826027ffbded762a7ce6263849627b260abf5aaa210746eaca0006"
      }
    },
    {
      "dom_id": "step-33986",
      "name": "Example: \n                    Calculating a Probability Involving a Sum or Difference of Normally Distributed Random Variables",
      "problem": "If $X_1\\sim N(10,3^2)$ and $X_2\\sim N(20,5^2)$ are independent and $Y=5X_1-4X_2,$ calculate $P(3 \\lt Y \\lt  40 ).$ Round your final answer to two decimal places.\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $\\Phi(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $\\Phi(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> <th width=\"25%\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$z$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$0.01$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$0.02$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$0.03$</th>\n</tr><tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\, 1.2 \\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $0.8869$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $0.8888$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $0.8907$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\, 1.3 \\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $0.9049$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $0.9066$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $0.9082$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\, 1.4 \\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $0.9207$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $0.9222$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $0.9236$ </td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</th>\n\n<th width=\"5%\"></th>\n\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> <th width=\"25%\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$z$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$0.00$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$0.01$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$0.02$</th>\n</tr><tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\, 2.7 \\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $0.9965$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $0.9966$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $0.9967$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\, 2.8 \\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $0.9974$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $0.9975$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $0.9976$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\, 2.9 \\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $0.9981$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $0.9982$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $0.9982$ </td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</th>\n</tr>\n\n</tbody></table>",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that if $X_1$ and $X_2$ are independent random variables, where $X_1\\sim N(\\mu_1,\\sigma^2_1)$ and $X_2\\sim N(\\mu_2,\\sigma^2_2),$ and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then \n\n$$\naX_1+bX_2\\sim N(a\\mu_1+b\\mu_2, a^2\\sigma^2_1+b^2\\sigma^2_2).\n$$\n\nSince $X_1$ and $X_2$ are independent, the distribution of $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y=5{X}_{1}-4{X}_{2} & ∼N(5{\\mu }_{1}-4{\\mu }_{2},{5}^{2}\\cdot {\\sigma }_{1}^{2}+{4}^{2}\\cdot {\\sigma }_{2}^{2}) \\\\  & ∼N(5{\\mu }_{1}-4{\\mu }_{2},25{\\sigma }_{1}^{2}+16{\\sigma }_{2}^{2}) \\\\  & ∼N(5\\cdot 10+(-4)\\cdot 20,25\\cdot {3}^{2}+16\\cdot {5}^{2}) \\\\  & ∼N(-30,625).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Y$ is normally distributed with mean $\\mu = -30$ and standard deviation $\\sigma = \\sqrt{625} = 25.$ \n\nWe want to find $P(3 \\lt Y \\lt  40).$ Thus, we convert $Y$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3<Y<40) & =P(\\frac{3-(-30)}{25}<Z<\\frac{40-(-30)}{25}) \\\\  & =P(1.32<Z<2.8) \\\\  & =P(Z<2.8)-P(Z<1.32) \\\\  & =Φ(2.8)-Φ(1.32)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the $z$-table, we see that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(1.32) & ≈0.9066 \\\\ Φ(2.8) & ≈0.9974.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3<Y<40) & =Φ(2.8)-Φ(1.32) \\\\  & ≈0.9974-0.9066 \\\\  & ≈0.09.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "html": "<div id=\"step-33986\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block\" stepid=\"33986\" steptype=\"example\" contentid=\"9118\">\n            <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                <div class=\"stepName\">\n                    Example: \n                    <a id=\"stepAnchor-33986\" class=\"stepAnchor\" style=\"font-weight: normal;\" name=\"step-9\">Calculating a Probability Involving a Sum or Difference of Normally Distributed Random Variables</a> \n                </div>      \n                <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"33986\">?</div>\n            </div>\n            \n            <div class=\"exampleQuestion\">\n                <style type=\"text/css\">\n                            .mjpage .MJX-monospace {\n                            font-family: monospace\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage .MJX-sans-serif {\n                            font-family: sans-serif\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage {\n                            display: inline;\n                            font-style: normal;\n                            font-weight: normal;\n                            line-height: normal;\n                            font-size: 100%;\n                            font-size-adjust: none;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            text-align: left;\n                            text-transform: none;\n                            letter-spacing: normal;\n                            word-spacing: normal;\n                            word-wrap: normal;\n                            white-space: nowrap;\n                            float: none;\n                            direction: ltr;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            padding: 0;\n      