      "html_path": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14275528/observations/step-e9103-8e26a32170e8ca41d975.html",
      "screenshot": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14275528/observations/step-e9103-8e26a32170e8ca41d975.png",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that if $X_1$ and $X_2$ are independent random variables, where $X_1\\sim N(\\mu_1,\\sigma^2_1)$ and $X_2\\sim N(\\mu_2,\\sigma^2_2),$ then \n\n$$\nY = X_1+X_2\\sim N(\\mu_1+\\mu_2, \\sigma^2_1+\\sigma^2_2).\n$$\n\nSince $X_1$ and $X_2$ are independent, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y={X}_{1}+{X}_{2} & ∼N(2+(-2),5+2) \\\\  & ∼N(0,7).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Y\\sim N(0, 7).$",
      "can_dont_know": false,
      "can_skip": false,
      "question": {
        "dom_id": "step-e9103",
        "name": "Example: Finding the Distribution of a Sum or Difference of Normal Random Variables",
        "problem": "If $X_1\\sim N(2,5)$ and $X_2\\sim  N(-2, 2)$ are independent, then what is the distribution of $Y = X_1+X_2?$",
        "worked_solution": "Recall that if $X_1$ and $X_2$ are independent random variables, where $X_1\\sim N(\\mu_1,\\sigma^2_1)$ and $X_2\\sim N(\\mu_2,\\sigma^2_2),$ then \n\n$$\nY = X_1+X_2\\sim N(\\mu_1+\\mu_2, \\sigma^2_1+\\sigma^2_2).\n$$\n\nSince $X_1$ and $X_2$ are independent, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y={X}_{1}+{X}_{2} & ∼N(2+(-2),5+2) \\\\  & ∼N(0,7).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Y\\sim N(0, 7).$",
        "calculator_instructions": "",
        "fields": [],
        "problem_field_keys": [],
        "answer_fields_complete": null,
        "result": null,
        "proof_feedback": null,
