      ],
      "html_path": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14275528/observations/step-e9119-987dbb3f39109a8c8d56.html",
      "screenshot": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14275528/observations/step-e9119-987dbb3f39109a8c8d56.png",
      "worked_solution": "Let $X$ denote the student's math test result, and let $Y$ denote the student's history test result. We want to find \n\n$$\nP( X+Y > 150).\n$$\n\nSince $X$ and $Y$ are  independent random variables such that $X\\sim N(67,12^2)$ and $Y\\sim N(73,9^2),$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X+Y & ∼N(67+73,{12}^{2}+{9}^{2}) \\\\  & ∼N(140,225).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nSo, the variable $X+Y$ is normally distributed with mean $\\mu = 140$ and standard deviation $\\sigma = \\sqrt{225} = 15.$\n\nIn order to find $P(X+Y > 150),$ we convert $X+Y$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X+Y>150) & =P(Z>\\frac{150-140}{15}) \\\\  & ≈P(Z>0.67) \\\\  & =1-P(Z\\le 0.67) \\\\  & =1-Φ(0.67)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the $z$-table, we see that\n\n$$\n\\Phi(0.67 )\\approx 0.7486.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X+Y>150) & ≈1-Φ(0.67) \\\\  & ≈1-0.7486 \\\\  & =0.2514.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that the probability that the combined score is more than $150$ is $0.2514.$",
      "can_dont_know": false,
      "can_skip": false,
      "question": {
        "dom_id": "step-e9119",
        "name": "Example: Calculating a Probability Involving a Sum or Difference of Normally Distributed Random Variables in Context",
        "problem": "The math test results of a group of students are normally distributed with a mean of $67$ and a standard deviation of $12.$ The results of the same group on a history test are normally distributed with a mean of $73$ and a standard deviation of $9.$ If one student is randomly selected, what is the probability their combined score from both tests is more than $150?$ You may assume that the student's scores on both tests are independent. \n\n*Hint: A table of values of $\\Phi(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $\\Phi(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $z$ | $\\, 0.05 \\,$ | $\\, 0.06 \\,$ | $\\, 0.07 \\,$ | $\\, 0.08 \\,$ | $\\, 0.09 \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\, 0.5 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7088 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7123 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7157 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7190 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7224 \\,$ |\n| $\\, 0.6 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7422 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7454 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7486 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7517 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7549 \\,$ |\n| $\\, 0.7 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7734 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7764 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7794 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7823 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7852 \\,$ |",
        "worked_solution": "Let $X$ denote the student's math test result, and let $Y$ denote the student's history test result. We want to find \n\n$$\nP( X+Y > 150).\n$$\n\nSince $X$ and $Y$ are  independent random variables such that $X\\sim N(67,12^2)$ and $Y\\sim N(73,9^2),$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X+Y & ∼N(67+73,{12}^{2}+{9}^{2}) \\\\  & ∼N(140,225).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nSo, the variable $X+Y$ is normally distributed with mean $\\mu = 140$ and standard deviation $\\sigma = \\sqrt{225} = 15.$\n\nIn order to find $P(X+Y > 150),$ we convert $X+Y$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X+Y>150) & =P(Z>\\frac{150-140}{15}) \\\\  & ≈P(Z>0.67) \\\\  & =1-P(Z\\le 0.67) \\\\  & =1-Φ(0.67)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the $z$-table, we see that\n\n$$\n\\Phi(0.67 )\\approx 0.7486.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X+Y>150) & ≈1-Φ(0.67) \\\\  & ≈1-0.7486 \\\\  & =0.2514.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that the probability that the combined score is more than $150$ is $0.2514.$",
        "calculator_instructions": "",
        "fields": [],
        "problem_field_keys": [],
        "answer_fields_complete": null,
        "result": null,
        "proof_feedback": null,
        "html": "<div id=\"step-e9119\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block;\">\n    \n                 \n                <div class=\"example\">\n                    <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                        <div class=\"stepName\"><span class=\"stepType\">Example:</span> Calculating a Probability Involving a Sum or Difference of Normally Distributed Random Variables in Context</div>       \n                        <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"e9119\">?</div>\n                    </div>\n            \n                    <div class=\"exampleQuestion\">\n                        <style type=\"text/css\">\n                            .mjpage .MJX-monospace {\n                            font-family: monospace\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage .MJX-sans-serif {\n                            font-family: sans-serif\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage {\n                            display: inline;\n                            font-style: normal;\n                            font-weight: normal;\n                            line-height: normal;\n                            font-size: 100%;\n                            font-size-adjust: none;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            text-align: left;\n                            text-transform: none;\n                            letter-spacing: normal;\n                            word-spacing: normal;\n                            word-wrap: normal;\n                            white-space: nowrap;\n                            float: none;\n                            direction: ltr;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            margin: 0\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage * {\n                            transition: none;\n                            -webkit-transition: none;\n                            -moz-transition: none;\n                            -ms-transition: none;\n                            -o-transition: none\n                            }\n\n                            .mjx-svg-href {\n                            fill: blue;\n                            stroke: blue\n                            }\n\n                            .MathJax_SVG_LineBox {\n                            display: table!important\n                            }\n\n                            .MathJax_SVG_LineBox span {\n                            display: table-cell!important;\n                            width: 10000em!important;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            margin: 0\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage__block {\n                            text-align: center;\n                            margin: 1em 0em;\n                            position: relative;\n                            display: block!important;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            width: 100%\n                            }</style><p>The math test results of a group of students are normally distributed with a mean of <span class=\"mjpage\"><svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"2.325ex\" height=\"2.176ex\" style=\"vertical-align: -0.338ex;\" viewBox=\"0 -791.3 1001 936.9\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-labelledby=\"MathJax-SVG-1-Title\">\n<title id=\"MathJax-SVG-