      "solution": {
        "status": "ambiguous",
        "reasoning": "Independence is not stated. The mean is 5, but the variance is 20+2Cov(X_1,X_2), and normal marginals alone do not guarantee a normal sum. Independent variables would give N(5,20); taking X_1=2+4Z and X_2=3+2Z with the same standard normal Z instead gives N(5,36). Therefore choice a is mathematically correct. The supplied worked example does not establish MA's answer to this question.",
        "confidence": 1,
        "answers": [
