      "solution": {
        "status": "ambiguous",
        "reasoning": "Independence is not stated. The mean is 2-3=-1, but the variance is 20-2Cov(X_1,X_2), and normal marginals alone do not guarantee a normal difference. Independent variables give N(-1,20), whereas X_1=2+4Z and X_2=3+2Z with the same standard normal Z give N(-1,4). Thus choice e is mathematically correct. No captured MA answer or grade establishes this question's key; the worked example concerns a different question.",
