            "transformation": null,
            "rendered_sha256": "b8c326b23c1c21c5f144ad1368ad5877001476da6c6af949c0377ec47c2381b5"
          }
        ],
        "html_path": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14275528/observations/step-q109729-2ae011e91db0a25cf2e0.html",
        "screenshot": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14275528/observations/step-q109729-2ae011e91db0a25cf2e0.png",
        "worked_solution": "Recall that if ${X}_{1}$ and ${X}_{2}$ are independent random variables, where ${X}_{1}∼N({\\mu }_{1},{\\sigma }_{1}^{2})$ and ${X}_{2}∼N({\\mu }_{2},{\\sigma }_{2}^{2}),$ and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then \n\n$$\na{X}_{1}+b{X}_{2}∼N(a{\\mu }_{1}+b{\\mu }_{2},{a}^{2}{\\sigma }_{1}^{2}+{b}^{2}{\\sigma }_{2}^{2}).\n$$\n\nSince ${X}_{1}$ and ${X}_{2}$ are independent, the distribution of $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y={X}_{1}-{X}_{2} & ∼N({\\mu }_{1}-{\\mu }_{2},{\\sigma }_{1}^{2}+{\\sigma }_{2}^{2}) \\\\  & ∼N(20-2,200+25) \\\\  & ∼N(18,225).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Y$ is normally distributed with mean $\\mu =18$ and standard deviation $\\sigma =\\sqrt{225}=15.$ \n\nWe want to find $P(Y>1.8).$ Thus, we convert $Y$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y>1.8) & =P(Z>\\frac{1.8-18}{15}) \\\\  & =P(Z>-1.08) \\\\  & =1-Φ(-1.08)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the $z$-table, we see that\n\n$$\nΦ(-1.08)≈0.1401.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y>1.8) & =1-Φ(-1.08) \\\\  & =1-0.1401 \\\\  & ≈0.86.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "can_dont_know": false,
        "can_skip": false,
        "question": {
          "dom_id": "step-q109729",
          "name": "Question 12",
          "problem": "If ${X}_{1}∼N(20,200)$ and ${X}_{2}∼N(2,25)$ are independent and $Y={X}_{1}-{X}_{2},$ calculate $P(Y>1.8).$ Round your final answer to two decimal places.\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ | $\\,0.09\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-1.2\\,$ | $\\,0.1056\\,$ | $\\,0.1038\\,$ | $\\,0.1020\\,$ | $\\,0.1003\\,$ | $\\,0.0985\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.1\\,$ | $\\,0.1251\\,$ | $\\,0.1230\\,$ | $\\,0.1210\\,$ | $\\,0.1190\\,$ | $\\,0.1170\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.0\\,$ | $\\,0.1469\\,$ | $\\,0.1446\\,$ | $\\,0.1423\\,$ | $\\,0.1401\\,$ | $\\,0.1379\\,$ |",
          "worked_solution": "Recall that if ${X}_{1}$ and ${X}_{2}$ are independent random variables, where ${X}_{1}∼N({\\mu }_{1},{\\sigma }_{1}^{2})$ and ${X}_{2}∼N({\\mu }_{2},{\\sigma }_{2}^{2}),$ and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then \n\n$$\na{X}_{1}+b{X}_{2}∼N(a{\\mu }_{1}+b{\\mu }_{2},{a}^{2}{\\sigma }_{1}^{2}+{b}^{2}{\\sigma }_{2}^{2}).\n$$\n\nSince ${X}_{1}$ and ${X}_{2}$ are independent, the distribution of $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y={X}_{1}-{X}_{2} & ∼N({\\mu }_{1}-{\\mu }_{2},{\\sigma }_{1}^{2}+{\\sigma }_{2}^{2}) \\\\  & ∼N(20-2,200+25) \\\\  & ∼N(18,225).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Y$ is normally distributed with mean $\\mu =18$ and standard deviation $\\sigma =\\sqrt{225}=15.$ \n\nWe want to find $P(Y>1.8).$ Thus, we convert $Y$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y>1.8) & =P(Z>\\frac{1.8-18}{15}) \\\\  & =P(Z>-1.08) \\\\  & =1-Φ(-1.08)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the $z$-table, we see that\n\n$$\nΦ(-1.08)≈0.1401.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y>1.8) & =1-Φ(-1.08) \\\\  & =1-0.1401 \\\\  & ≈0.86.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "calculator_instructions": "",
          "fields": [
            {
              "key": "selection",
              "type": "radio",
              "choices": [
                {
                  "option": "a",
                  "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-109729-a",
                  "type": "math",
                  "value": "0.88",
                  "html": "<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"265\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2E\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c38\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c38\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0.88</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>"
                },
                {
                  "option": "b",
                  "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-109729-b",
