      "solution": {
        "status": "ambiguous",
        "reasoning": "Independence gives Y a normal distribution with mean 7-8=-1 and variance 5+4=9, so its standard deviation is 3. The standardized bounds are (-1.9+1)/3=-0.30 and (-0.49+1)/3=0.17. Therefore the probability is Φ(0.17)-Φ(-0.30)=0.5675-0.3821=0.1854, which rounds to 0.19, choice a. No captured MA answer or grade establishes this question's key; the worked example concerns a different question.",
        "confidence": 1,
