    {
      "key": "step-q110331",
      "question": {
        "dom_id": "step-q110331",
        "name": "Question 16",
        "problem": "A particular shop sells chicken eggs and quail eggs. The weight of a chicken egg is normally distributed with a mean of $64\\,\\text{g}$ and a standard deviation of $5\\,\\text{g}.$ The weight of a quail egg is normally distributed with a mean of $14\\,\\text{g}$ and a standard deviation of $1\\,\\text{g}.$ If one chicken egg and one quail egg are randomly selected, what is the probability that the weight of the chicken egg is more than $5$ times greater than the weight of the quail egg? You may assume that the weights are independent.\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ | $\\,0.09\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.7734\\,$ | $\\,0.7764\\,$ | $\\,0.7794\\,$ | $\\,0.7823\\,$ | $\\,0.7852\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.8023\\,$ | $\\,0.8051\\,$ | $\\,0.8078\\,$ | $\\,0.8106\\,$ | $\\,0.8133\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.9\\,$ | $\\,0.8289\\,$ | $\\,0.8315\\,$ | $\\,0.8340\\,$ | $\\,0.8365\\,$ | $\\,0.8389\\,$ |",
        "worked_solution": "Let $X$ denote the weight of a chicken egg, and let $Y$ denote the weight of a quail egg. We want to find \n\n$$\nP(X>5Y)=P(X-5Y>0).\n$$\n\nSince $X$ and $Y$ are  independent random variables such that $X∼N(64,{5}^{2})$ and $Y∼N(14,{1}^{2})$, then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X-5Y & ∼N(64-5\\cdot 14,25+{5}^{2}\\cdot 1) \\\\  & ∼N(-6,50).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variable $X-5Y$ is normally distributed with mean $\\mu =-6$ and standard deviation $\\sigma =\\sqrt{50}.$\n\nIn order to find $P(X-5Y>0),$ we convert $X-5Y$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X-5Y>0) & =P(Z>\\frac{0+6}{\\sqrt{50}}) \\\\  & ≈P(Z>0.85) \\\\  & =1-P(Z<0.85) \\\\  & =1-P(Z\\le 0.85) \\\\  & =1-Φ(0.85)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the $z$-table, we see that\n\n$$\nΦ(0.85)≈0.8023.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X-5Y>0) & ≈1-Φ(0.85) \\\\  & ≈1-0.8023 \\\\  & ≈0.1977.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that the probability that the weight of a chicken egg is more than $5$ times greater than the weight of a quail egg is $0.1977.$",
        "calculator_instructions": "",
